==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*peh₃-}}
From {{inh-lite|en|enm|poisoun}}, {{m-lite|enm|poyson}}, {{m-lite|enm|poysone}}, {{m-lite|enm|puyson}}, {{m-lite|enm|puisun}}, from {{der-lite|en|fro|poison}}, {{m-lite|fro|poison}}, from {{der-lite|en|la|potio|pōtio, pōtiōnis|t=drink, a draught, a poisonous draught, a potion}}, from {{m-lite|la|poto|pōtō|t=I drink}}. See also {{doublet|en|potion|notext=1}} and {{m-lite|en|potable}}.

Displaced native {{noncog-lite|ang|ator|ātor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|poi'zən}}, {{IPA-lite|en|/ˈpɔɪz(ə)n/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-poison.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes-lite|en|ɔɪzən|s=2}}
* {{hyph-lite|en|poi|son}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[substance]] that is [[harmful]] or [[lethal]] to a living organism when ingested.
#: {{ux-lite|en|We used a '''poison''' to kill the weeds.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Anything [[harmful]] to a person or thing.
#: {{ux-lite|en|Gossip is a malicious '''poison'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Jack Straw|IV|87|Awaie with the Rebels ſuffer them not to ſpeake,<br>His words are '''poyſon''' in the eares of the people, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An intoxicating [[drink]]; a [[liquor]]. (note: this sense is chiefly encountered in the phrases "name your poison" and "what's your poison ?")
#: ''— What's your '''poison'''?''
#: ''— I'll have a glass of whiskey.''
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Any substance that [[inhibit]]s [[catalytic]] [[activity]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Huazhang Liu|title=Ammonia Synthesis Catalysts: Innovation and Practice|page=693
|passage=The temperature effect of '''poisons'''. The influence of '''poison''' on the catalyst can be different with the change of reaction conditions.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Not to be confused with [[venom#Noun|venom]]''

