===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To use poison to [[kill]] or [[paralyse]] (somebody).
#: {{ux-lite|en|The assassin '''poisoned''' the king.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[pollute]]; to cause to become [[poisonous]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|That factory is '''poisoning''' the river.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to become much [[worse]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|Suspicion will '''poison''' their relationship.}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|He '''poisoned''' the mood in the room with his non-stop criticism.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause (someone) to [[hate]] or to have [[unfair]] [[negative]] [[opinion]]s.
#: {{ux-lite|en|She's '''poisoned''' him against all his old friends.}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} To [[inhibit]] the [[catalytic]] [[activity]] of.
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To place [[false]] [[information]] into (a [[cache]]) as part of an [[exploit]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Ronald L. Mendell|title=Investigating Information-based Crimes|page=93
|passage=In this technique, the hacker '''poisons''' the cache to launch malware into Web pages.}}

